      "message": "If I\u0027m reading this correctly, the current code sends callbacks to a socket even if it was rebound / disconnected / reconnected / etc. after the callback was first registered (because validate is only called when the callback is registered).\n\nIs this an information leakage bug that allows apps to get callbacks for sockets they don\u0027t own. If so, that seems like perhaps it\u0027s something we should fix in S as well?\n\nIf you think it\u0027s disruptive to send the onError callback, then maybe you could simply drop the event, or drop the event and unregister the callback but not send the onError callback.\n\nLGTM either way.",
